                     <title>J. Gadesden, Rosa medicinae</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Flyleaves (formerly pasted down) from a
                        homiliary well written in Enlish hand of c. 1000 (fols. 1, 286).</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">2o folio (fol. 10r): 'et sanguis qui
                        fiet'.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Mark of chain on fols. 1--5 at head.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">William Romsey was fellow of Merton 1448, gave
                        3 books to Merton in 1493 and MS Oriel 6 to Oriel. Merton MSS. 47 and Oriel
                        6 were written at Romsey's cost ('quem fieri fecit').</note>
                  </msItem>
